 "answer": "**At the latest reading I could verify—8:00 a.m. MYT today, October 17—the KL API was 161, which is “unhealthy.”** ([semakapi.my](https://semakapi.my/en/kuala-lumpur))\n\nIf your children have asthma or other breathing problems, are already coughing or wheezing, or would spend much time outdoors getting to school, **keeping them home today is a reasonable choice**—Malaysia’s Education Minister has said parents may do so over health concerns if they notify the school. ([web26.bernama.com](https://web26.bernama.com/en/general/news.php?id=2620854))\n\nIf they’re generally healthy and the school confirms they’ll stay indoors, **going in may be reasonable**, but outdoor activities should be stopped once API exceeds 100; the school-closure threshold is 200 under the current guidance. ([web26.bernama.com](https://web26.bernama.com/en/general/news.php?id=2620854)) Check the school’s messages and the latest nearby APIMS reading before deciding, since the index can change.",
